## Why MIT?

An educational repository should be maximally reusable: teachers should be able to
print chapters, translate them, remix them into a course, or bundle them into a
static site without legal friction. MIT permits all of that with a single
attribution requirement and no copyleft obligation, which is why it is the default
for open educational content of this kind.

Content and diagrams are covered by the same licence. Third-party material quoted
for scholarly purposes (for example a figure description adapted from a textbook)
remains the property of its original authors and is attributed in place.
